<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; Arrows Puzzle</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
  <SideAd />
    <h1>Arrows Puzzle: How to Play, Full Rules, and Beginner Tips</h1>

    <p class="lede">You have probably seen <strong>Arrows – Puzzle Escape</strong> near the top of the Play Store charts: a clean white board, arrows sitting on a twisting path, and three hearts watching you from the top of the screen. Below are the real rules, a visual demo of the one move that matters, six strategies, and straight answers to the questions players ask most.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Lessmore GmbH.</div>

    <h2>What Is the Arrows Puzzle?</h2>
    <p><strong>Arrows – Puzzle Escape</strong> is a minimalist logic game by <strong>Lessmore GmbH</strong> for Android and iOS, with more than <strong>100 million</strong> downloads and a 4.7-star rating on Google Play. Arrows sit on a grid path, and you tap one to slide it out of the board in the direction it points — the goal is to extract every arrow without a collision. It is a game of reading paths and empty space, not of speed: there is no timer.</p>

    <h2>How the Arrows Puzzle Works</h2>
    <div class="rulewrap">
      <div class="xdemo" id="xdemo"></div>
      <ol>
        <li><b>Tap an arrow and it slides out of the board.</b> The arrow moves in the direction it points, along the path, until it leaves the grid.</li>
        <li><b>Collisions cost hearts.</b> If another arrow stands in the slide path, the two arrows collide — you lose 1 of your 3 hearts. (In the demo: the green arrow has a clear path to the edge; the red ✕ arrow is blocked.)</li>
        <li><b>Double-headed arrows have two exits.</b> Tap them and you can choose which of the two directions they slide out — usually the safer one.</li>
        <li><b>Clear the grid without losing a single heart.</b> That is the goal of every level. Hints exist for stuck moments; the timer does not.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="callout grn"><span><b>The whole game in one sentence:</b> never tap an arrow whose slide path still has an arrow on it — find arrows with empty paths and pull them out first.</span></div>

    <h2>6 Arrows Puzzle Strategies</h2>
    <div class="strat">
      <div class="st"><i>1</i><span><b>Slide the arrows whose path is already empty first.</b> Scan every arrow before touching anything; each arrow that can leave without hitting anything is a guaranteed safe move — bank it immediately.</span></div>
      <div class="st"><i>2</i><span><b>Clear from the outside in.</b> Arrows near the edge have short slide paths and few possible blockers. Peel the rim first and the interior becomes far less tangled.</span></div>
      <div class="st"><i>3</i><span><b>Count the blockers.</b> If an arrow is blocked by exactly one other arrow, that blocker is your next target: slide it out first and the arrow behind it becomes a free tap.</span></div>
      <div class="st"><i>4</i><span><b>Favor arrows pointing at an empty edge.</b> When an arrow faces a straight, clear run to the board edge, it is guaranteed to escape — take it before the layout shifts.</span></div>
      <div class="st"><i>5</i><span><b>Treat double-headed arrows as escape doors.</b> When a double arrow is the only thing trapping a neighbor, try both of its exits and pick the direction that frees the most arrows with the least risk.</span></div>
      <div class="st"><i>6</i><span><b>Manage hearts, not speed.</b> There is no timer, so uncertainty is never an emergency. A collision costs a heart; re-planning costs a second — think before you tap.</span></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Real Boards: Official Screenshots</h2>
    <div class="snaprow">
      <figure><img src="/arrows-puzzle/board-1.jpg" alt="Arrows – Puzzle Escape official screenshot: a knight-shaped arrow path with three hearts at the top of the screen" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Official board · arrow maze</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/arrows-puzzle/board-2.jpg" alt="Arrows – Puzzle Escape official screenshot: a dense rounded arrow path with three hearts and no timer visible" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Official board · dense path</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <p>Notice what both boards share: arrows packed along a single winding path, three hearts at the top, and no countdown clock. Every level is a variation on that shape — longer paths, more arrows, tighter corners — and the same extraction logic applies throughout.</p>


    <h2>How This Guide Compares</h2>
    <p>Not all Arrows – Puzzle Escape guides are built the same. Here is what each kind of resource actually gives you, so you can pick the right one for the question you have right now.</p>
    <table class="cmp">
      <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>What you get</th><th>Watch out for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>This guide</th><td>Rules verified against the official store listing and real gameplay footage, official board screenshots, a field-tested solving method, and straight answers on hearts, hints, and level counts.</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Official store listing</th><td>The accurate feature list, straight from Lessmore GmbH.</td><td>Marketing copy only — no strategy, no board reading.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Video walkthroughs</th><td>A real tap-by-tap move order for one specific board.</td><td>Can't be scanned or searched, ad breaks mid-solve, and you have to scrub a timeline to find the move you need.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Auto-generated guide sites</th><td>One page per level number, quick to index.</td><td>The same generic tips recycled on every level, no real board data, and sometimes features the game doesn't actually have.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="cmp-note">If the game doesn't have a feature, we don't describe it. If a number isn't published by the developer, we say so instead of inventing one.</p>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details><summary>How many levels are in Arrows Puzzle Escape?</summary><p>Arrows – Puzzle Escape has thousands of handcrafted levels per the official listing, plus a daily challenge that keeps adding fresh boards. The developer has not published an exact total. The official difficulty ladder runs Normal, Hard, Super Hard, and Nightmare.</p></details>

    <details><summary>Who makes Arrows Puzzle Escape?</summary><p>Arrows – Puzzle Escape is made by Lessmore GmbH. It is free to play on Android and iOS, with over 100 million downloads and a 4.7-star rating on Google Play.</p></details>

    <details><summary>How do hearts work in Arrows Puzzle Escape?</summary><p>You start each level with 3 hearts. Tapping an arrow whose slide path is blocked by another arrow causes a collision and costs one heart. The goal is to clear the grid without losing a single heart, and because there is no timer there is never a reason to risk a careless tap.</p></details>

    <details><summary>Does Arrows Puzzle Escape have hints?</summary><p>Yes. Arrows – Puzzle Escape has a built-in hint system for when a board deadlocks. Since collisions cost hearts, using a hint is usually cheaper than guessing into a blocked path.</p></details>

    <details><summary>Is there a timer in Arrows Puzzle Escape?</summary><p>No. Arrows – Puzzle Escape has no timer — the only pressure is your three hearts. You can study any board for as long as you like before tapping an arrow.</p></details>

    <details><summary>Is Arrows Puzzle Escape free?</summary><p>Yes. Arrows – Puzzle Escape is a free-to-play mobile game with ads on Google Play and the App Store, with over 100 million downloads. It is not available as an official browser game — the exact levels are mobile-only.</p></details>

